 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "nhé y đi (órdenes y propuestas amables)",
    "@en": "nhe and đi (friendly orders and proposals)"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**đi** al final convierte la frase en una orden o un «¡venga!»: **Thức dậy đi!** = ¡levántate!",
     "@en": "**đi** in the end turns the phrase into an order or a «Come on!»: **Thức dậy đi!** = get up!"
    },
    {
     "@es": "**nhé** al final es más suave, como «¿vale?»: sirve para proponer o pedir algo, y es mejor con personas mayores: **Đi ăn phở với tôi nhé** = vamos a comer phở, ¿vale?",
     "@en": "**nhé** in the end it's softer, like «¿vale?»: serves to propose or ask for something, and is better with older people: **Đi ăn phở với tôi nhé** = let's eat phởOkay?"
    },
    {
     "@es": "También se usa al dar las gracias: **Cảm ơn nhé!**",
     "@en": "It is also used when thanking: **Cảm ơn nhé!**"
    },
    {
     "@es": "¡Importante! Sin **đi** o **nhé**, una orden suena brusca y mandona.",
     "@en": "Important! Without **đi** or **nhé**, an order sounds abrupt and mandonous."
    }
   ]
  },
